  "worked_solution": "The quotient rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot g(x)-f(x)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(2)=\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(2)\\cdot g(2)-f(2)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(2)}{(g(2))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(2)=3$ and $g(2)=-2.$\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (1,3)$ equals $0.$ So, ${f}^{\u2032}(2)=0.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (1,3)$ equals $2.$ So, ${g}^{\u2032}(2)=2.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2032}(2) & =\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(2)\\cdot g(2)-f(2)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(2)}{(g(2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 2}{{(-2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
